{"name":"Tern Grey","hex":"#d5cdbd","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tern","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various seabirds of the subfamily Sterninae (of the family Laridae) that are similar to gulls but are smaller and have a forked tail."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thing with three components; a set of three things.\n A lottery prize resulting from the favourable combination of three numbers in the draw.","A lottery prize resulting from the favourable combination of three numbers in the draw."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tern"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tern","blocks":[{"text":"Terns are seabirds in the subfamily Sterninae of the wider gull and tern family Laridae. They have a worldwide distribution and are normally found near the sea, rivers, or wetlands. Terns are treated in eleven genera in a subgroup of the family Laridae, which also includes several genera of gulls and the skimmers (Rynchops). They are slender, lightly built birds with long, forked tails, narrow wings, long bills, and relatively short legs. Most species are pale grey above and white below with a contrasting black cap to the head, but the marsh terns, the black-bellied tern, the Inca tern, and some noddies have dark body plumage for at least part of the year. The sexes are identical in appearance, but young birds are readily distinguishable from adults. Terns have a non-breeding plumage, which usually involves a white forehead and much-reduced black cap."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/3-point_tern_%28Sandwich%2C_Common_%26_Roseate_Terns%2C_St_Mary%27s_Island%2C_Northumberland%29.jpg/330px-3-point_tern_%28Sandwich%2C_Common_%26_Roseate_Terns%2C_St_Mary%27s_Island%2C_Northumberland%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tern","wikidata":"Q33140745"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Birds_of_Sweden_2016_07.jpg/500px-Birds_of_Sweden_2016_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Birds_of_Sweden_2016_07.jpg/1280px-Birds_of_Sweden_2016_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Birds_of_Sweden_2016_07.jpg/500px-Birds_of_Sweden_2016_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Common tern in flight","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABirds_of_Sweden_2016_07.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Birds_of_Sweden_2016_08.jpg/500px-Birds_of_Sweden_2016_08.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Birds_of_Sweden_2016_08.jpg/500px-Birds_of_Sweden_2016_08.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Common tern in flight","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABirds_of_Sweden_2016_08.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thum